      "heading_context": "## Gotchas from C#",
      "headers": [
        "C# behavior",
        "TypeScript behavior",
        "Consequence"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Nominal types: `Dog != Cat` even if same shape",
          "Structural types: same shape = same type",
          "Different mental model"
        ],
        [
          "Runtime type checking via reflection",
          "No runtime types — types erased",
          "`instanceof` only works for classes"
        ],
        [
          "`interface` is a contract",
          "`interface` describes shape, no vtable",
          "TS interfaces work at compile time only"
        ],
        [
          "`null` is one thing",
          "`null` and `undefined` are different",
          "Need both: `T \\| null \\| undefined`"
        ],
        [
          "Generics reified at runtime",
          "Generics erased — no `T` at runtime",
          "Can't do `new T()` or check `is T`"
        ],
        [
          "`as` is a safe cast (throws if wrong)",
          "`as` is a type assertion (no runtime check)",
          "TypeScript `as` can lie"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
